  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Blue Fairness and Integrity Research Compact &#x2013; Year 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project works towards defining a standardized United Nations measurement framework for trafficking for forced labour. This is the second year of implementation and will focus on the finalization and validation of the survey tools, it also targets practitioners in charge of the identification of potential victims of trafficking for forced labour in the fishing industry. Based on the work on survey tool from the first year of implementation, and on the full-size pilot of the questionnaire, a group of experts and practitioners from developing countries will be called to work on the possible use of the questions and criteria used in the survey for their work, in particular to see how these criteria can be operationalized to improve detection of trafficking for forced labour in the fishing industry. The project is to be implemented though collaboration between UNODC, ILO, and IOM. IOM will contribute technical expertise across all activities, including the piloting of survey tools; convening a workshop to validate the tools; and, development of recommendations for their operationalization.</narrative>
  </description>
